  "notes": "LUMA Hotel San Francisco, 100 Channel St (at the corner of Channel and 3rd Streets, per Hoodline's 2018 groundbreaking report) -- a 299-room independent hotel with a rooftop bar on its 17th floor (the 2018 groundbreaking coverage gave 16 stories, Hoodline, or 17, SF Chronicle), developed by SOMA Hotel, a Stanford Hotel affiliate (Hoodline, 2018), architect Hornberger + Worstell with Cole Martinez Curtis & Associates (interiors), opened June 2022 as Mission Bay's first hotel. Confirmed inside the Mission Bay South project area: this parcel's zoning district in DataSF's Assessor parcel data is 'MISSION BAY REDEVELOPMENT' (zoning code MB-RA), and it sits on the Mission Bay South side of the Channel St boundary in DataSF's official redevelopment-area layer.",
